# Build intermediates. Source/Directory.Build.props sends them to ../.build/, outside Mod/: the
# Workshop uploader takes that folder as it stands on disk, with no filtering, so an obj/ left
# inside it would redistribute the publicised Assembly-CSharp.dll to every subscriber. The two
# in-place entries are belt and braces, for a build run with the props file bypassed.
.build/
Source/obj/
Source/bin/

# Claude Code session worktrees and local settings. A session creates its worktree in the current
# directory, so sometimes inside this one, and each is a full copy of the repository. Until this
# mod was detached, only the machine-wide ignore rule covered this - a property of the machine,
# not of the repository, which is why it is written here now.
.claude/

# Development environments.
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.csproj.user

# Windows shortcuts dropped in the mod folder, never content.
*.lnk

# System.
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Fiches de vitrine : elles ne sont pas publiables, et PUBLISHING.md demande de les effacer
# une fois Preview.png et ModIcon.png faits. A tout niveau, pas seulement a la racine.
PROMPT_*.md
**/PROMPT_*.md

# Pickle run captures are large and not evidence by themselves: the summary, the junit report, the
# log and the (small) films of a run are kept, the full-size stills stay on the machine.
Tests/Pickle/runs/*/captures/
Tests/Pickle/runs/*/small/
Tests/Pickle/runs/*/sheets/
